You're off to a good start, some comments:

MB, even at +0, qualifies as "extra nasty", and quivered daggers are
nothing to sneeze at.  It also looks like you have a very healthy
collection of attack spells, but no healing spells.  Whether or not to
advance either dagger or attack spells from skilled to expert should be
dependant on spell failure rates of other spell schools and your
reliance on those spells.

For combat strategy, I'd primarily use FB/DL followed by daggers at
range.  MM/CoC are better, and worth using when there is no danger of
getting either your self or your Minotaur on the rebound.

Try to ID the rest of your kit w/ the spell asap, you may have
something very useful sitting in inventory.

> Possible next steps:
>    Pray/Sac fest on altar w/CM (too slow w/o Eye).  Hope for +oPoly and
> try piling for missing gear.  Crowning would solve resistance problem.

One or two pre-quest go-arounds is probably worth it.  Do this *after*
dipping for a wish.  You don't want to limit your wish options by
getting an artifact weapon you don't really need.

>    Peaceful gray dragon in mines end for scales.  Worried about
> minotaur a little and conduct w/ peaceful, low % of scales and no EA to
> convert them.

+0 scales are better than your +1 leather.  They confer an intrinsic
and weigh less too!  The alignment penalty is a meaningless.

>    Sink on DL3: got the ring and danced a few times with the incubus.
> Could dance some more and/or start a small pudding farm for the scrolls
> and potions that I sorely lack, XP for quest, ShockR and CR.

I've never been one for farming myself, but exploit it for (at least)
the resistances.

>    Grab my =oPC and poly into a silver dragon, lay eggs, raise babies
> to adult, get them killed for scales (not very motherly).

But oh so worth it.

>    Dip in fountains for a wish of +2 SDSM.

If the only artifact you've seen is Magicbane, perhaps a co-aligned
quest artifact might be better.  (PYEC, Eyes of the Overworld, Master
Key of Thievery, &c).  Do this before you hit the quest or altar camp.

>    Do castle (worried about L, h and D).

Both 'L' and 'h' respect Elbereth, and can be found using telepathy.
You do have a blindfold/towel right?  MR, which you have, protects
against much of what 'L' can do to you.  Of those three, I think 'D'
are, by far, the most dangerous (especially the black ones, doubly so
without reflection).

A good bet would be to do all of the above, in the following order:
1) Dip for a wish
2) Kill peaceful gray dragon for scales
3) Raise silver dragons for scales
4) Do castle
5) Atlar camp for books/prot/weapons/luck
6) Farm puddings.

Short circuit and do the quest once you have reflection, a 2nd
artifact, and enough experience.  The Eye is just too useful.

> Key issues - AC is good but not great since ?oEA have been lacking,

It's good enough that I wouldn't stress it.  Intrinsics are more
important than AC in the pre-castle came anyways.  You have an
in-exhaustable, fast, and slow-eroding source of Elbereth.  Very few
*really* dangerous monsters don't respect that, and your dreadnought^W
Minotaur will help you wade through the remaining nasties.

> daggers at +0 due to lack of ?oEW

+0 is more than enough.  With a Wizard, I see thrown daggers as (at
best) my third or fourth option when it comes to combat.

> No reflection, Soko was BoH

This is your biggest issue, hands down.  Until you resolve it,
*religously* check for dragons.  If you see a black one, be somewhere
else.  I've lost not one, but *two* very ascendable characters to black
dragons while deep in Gehennom.

> Plenty of missing resistances

(Mostly) solveable by farming puddings or (intentional?) crowning.

> Sundry equipment missing like HoB, Speed boots, GoD, magic whistle,
> =oTC, Conflict, nothing Geno'd, no HP/Eng boosts,

Unless you have high failure rates and fewer than 3 non-cloak sources
of MR (wielding MB and carrying the Eye provide 2), the HoB is more of
a luxary than a necessity.  A robe + cornuthum may be more useful.

General consensus seems to be that jumping boots are more valueable
than speed boots.

Any old non-fumbling leather gloves are spellcaster friendly, enchanted
GoDex happen to be more friendly.  If you have (near) zero failure
rates for all your high-level spells w/o them, then they're probably
not worth wishing for.

You'll get intrinsic warning (XP:15) and TC (XP:17) eventually, so
don't sweat either (and don't gremlin dance).

Unless you lose your pet Minotaur, conflict is more dangerous for you
than for others.

Of those, only ?Geno and HoB are worth using castle wishes for.

HP/Eng boosts:  Either you get them or you don't.  If you do, great.
If you don't, don't stress about it.  Once you get a healing spell,
bless your !EH, alchemize them to !FH, then quaff.

